# The built-in permission sets a protected install's management identity holds by design, on every
# cloud. No set is exempt from the allow-lists because of its id: a set that is not listed here, or
# that differs from the built-in set of its id, is checked against the cloud's allow-list file
# (`aws.allow`, `azure.allow`, `gcp.allow`) like a set the stack defines. Setup's preflight adds
# the sets below to the management profile; what each grants is reviewed separately, and the
# verifier-owned filters (`verifier_owned.rs`) still drop whatever only the verifier may do.
#
# Format: `held <id or pattern>  # reason` and `unheld <id>  # reason`. A `*` matches any run of
# characters. An `unheld` line removes a set the `held` lines would otherwise cover. Every line
# needs a reason.

held */provision                       # a Live resource's create, update and delete after setup
held */management                      # a Frozen resource's ongoing management
held */heartbeat                       # health reads
held worker/dispatch-command           # sends a command to a worker through its queue
held queue/storage-notifications       # wires a Live queue to storage notifications
held queue/batch-metadata              # reads queue batch metadata
held storage/trigger-management        # manages a storage account's event subscriptions
held storage/remote-data-write         # writes the stack's storage on behalf of a remote caller
held sandbox/templates                 # a Frozen GCP sandbox's template
held sandbox/images                    # a Frozen Azure sandbox's disk images
held postgres/key-recovery             # recovers a database's key
held key/availability                  # checks a customer key's availability
held key/native-volume-management      # manages a native volume's key use
held vault/data-read                   # reads the stack's own vault secrets; `signed-` secrets are excluded by the grant's conditions
held vault/data-write                  # writes the stack's own vault secrets; `signed-` secrets are excluded by the grant's conditions
held observe/observe                   # reads and writes telemetry

unheld remote-stack-management/provision  # lets a role rewrite the management policies themselves: setup's, never management's
